stage: ssa (amplification; gets past parse + CFG, dies in SSA build)
kind: OOM (libFuzzer rss exceeded 2 GiB default limit)
site: parse → Cfg::build → SsaBody::build — no single panic location
repro: cargo fuzz run fuzz_ssa fuzz/crashes/fuzz_ssa/oom-6772da4a3bbd
size: 2347 bytes

Second fuzz_ssa OOM (distinct from oom-5263e994fb0c, which was 1841
bytes). Gets further than the prior one — completes CFG construction
before dying in the Braun name-resolution / phi-insertion phase of
SSA build. Likely drives phi node count off block count, which is
itself inflated by the same count-field amplification as the cfg OOMs.

Filed for `dex-hardening-sweep`. Root cause probably shares an
upstream fix with the three other OOMs: bound parse-time entity
counts against `data.len()`. A secondary SSA-side defense would be a
per-method phi-node count cap that rejects obviously pathological
join structures before allocation.
